of the hot volcanic springs where water bubbles up from deep below the surface

00:46:40.080 --> 00:46:45.240
of the brown bringing up a solution of soda and salt to trickle down and

00:46:45.240 --> 00:46:51.640
crystallize out in the lakes. You could hardly imagine a less likely place to

00:46:51.640 --> 00:46:57.360
find a fish.

00:46:57.360 --> 00:47:05.920
And yet there it is a species of tilapia. The water here can be as high as 43

00:47:05.920 --> 00:47:10.920
degrees centigrade 110 degrees Fahrenheit. Algae managed to grow here and

00:47:10.920 --> 00:47:17.680
the fish survive by feeding on it. Yet another niche a most unlikely one has

00:47:17.680 --> 00:47:25.240
been filled by the incredibly adaptable fishes. At the other extreme there is one

00:47:25.240 --> 00:47:34.640
fish in the coldest waters on earth.

00:47:34.640 --> 00:47:39.880
Seawater freezes below the temperature of freshwater. The ice fish from the

00:47:39.880 --> 00:47:44.280
seas of the Antarctic has developed a substance in its blood which keeps it

00:47:44.280 --> 00:47:50.000
liquid even when the seawater above it freezes solid. It has in fact a kind of

00:47:50.000 --> 00:47:59.240
antifreeze. But if one wanted to pick out of the 30,000 or so species of fish

00:47:59.240 --> 00:48:06.120
alive today the king of them all my vote would go to this the salmon.

00:48:06.120 --> 00:48:14.240
In the acuteness of its senses, the skillfulness of its navigation, the

00:48:14.240 --> 00:48:19.240
strength and athleticism of its body this surely must be a paragon among fish.

00:48:19.240 --> 00:48:24.360
In the Pacific there are several different kinds. They spend much of their

00:48:24.360 --> 00:48:29.360
time in the ocean feeding on plankton and small fish but in the summer they

00:48:29.360 --> 00:48:33.520
assemble off the North American coast and then they begin to battle their way

00:48:33.520 --> 00:48:41.560
up the rivers. Even falls don't stop them. The flexible rod that first appeared in

00:48:41.560 --> 00:48:45.960
the young sea squirt is here marvelously muscled and strengthened with a jointed

00:48:45.960 --> 00:48:51.520
column of bone. So with a thrash of its hind end and fins, movement first

00:48:51.520 --> 00:48:56.040
developed by the earliest ancestors of the fish, the salmon can swim and leap

00:48:56.040 --> 00:49:03.640
up the fastest tides and its lateral line can sense the details of the surge.

00:49:15.960 --> 00:49:21.720
The salmon's sense of smell is almost unbelievably acute. This river is not

00:49:21.720 --> 00:49:26.600
just any river, it is the precise one in which all these fish were hatched. Each

00:49:26.600 --> 00:49:31.840
has retained a memory of the taste and smell of these waters and this has

00:49:31.840 --> 00:49:36.200
drawn them back across thousands of miles of ocean so that they may complete

00:49:36.200 --> 00:49:40.040
their lives where they began them.

00:49:40.040 --> 00:49:53.160
During the past few days their bodies have been changing with astonishing

00:49:53.160 --> 00:50:00.160
speed. These pink salmon have developed high humped back with thin bodies and

00:50:00.160 --> 00:50:07.200
their lower jaws have become hooked. The front teeth of the males have developed

00:50:07.200 --> 00:50:13.360
into long and powerful fangs, hopeless for feeding but then the time of

00:50:13.360 --> 00:50:42.600
feeding is long since over. Their teeth are for battle.

00:50:43.440 --> 00:50:52.240
The males fight for a scrape scooped in the gravel of the riverbed. When one

00:50:52.240 --> 00:50:58.480
